# Service-Specific Implementation Patterns

> **Service Type Guidelines**  
> This rule defines specific implementation patterns for different types of services in the Logistics Aggregator Portal, based on their business domains and responsibilities.

## **User Service Implementation Patterns**

### **Core Responsibilities**

- User profile management
- Client organization management
- File upload handling (avatars, documents)
- User preferences and settings

### **Specific Schema Patterns**

```prisma
// User Service Schema (backend/user-service/prisma/schema.prisma)
model User {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  email       String   @unique
  firstName   String
  lastName    String
  phone       String?
  avatar      String?  // File path or URL
  role        Role     @default(CLIENT)
  clientId    String?  // For multi-tenant support
  isActive    Boolean  @default(true)
  preferences Json?    // User preferences
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt

  // Relationships
  client      Client?  @relation(fields: [clientId], references: [id])
  documents   UserDocument[]
  auditLogs   AuditLog[]

  @@map("users")
}

model Client {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  name         String
  domain       String?  @unique // For white-label
  logo         String?
  settings     Json?    // Client-specific settings
  isActive     Boolean  @default(true)
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime @updatedAt

  // Relationships
  users        User[]

  @@map("clients")
}

model UserDocument {
  id          String      @id @default(cuid())
  userId      String
  fileName    String
  filePath    String
  fileSize    Int
  mimeType    String
  documentType DocumentType
  createdAt   DateTime    @default(now())

  // Relationships
  user        User        @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@map("user_documents")
}

enum DocumentType {
  AVATAR
  ID_PROOF
  ADDRESS_PROOF
  BUSINESS_LICENSE
  OTHER
}
```

### **File Upload Controller Pattern**

```javascript
// controllers/userController.js - File upload handling
static async uploadAvatar(req, res) {
  try {
    const userId = req.user.userId;
    const file = req.file; // Multer middleware

    // Validate file
    if (!file) {
      return res.status(400).json({
        status: 'error',
        message: 'No file uploaded',
        code: 'FILE_REQUIRED'
      });
    }

    // File size and type validation
    const maxSize = parseInt(process.env.MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE) || 10485760; // 10MB
    const allowedTypes = (process.env.ALLOWED_FILE_TYPES || 'jpg,jpeg,png').split(',');

    if (file.size > maxSize) {
      return res.status(400).json({
        status: 'error',
        message: 'File size too large',
        code: 'FILE_TOO_LARGE'
      });
    }

    const fileExt = file.originalname.split('.').pop().toLowerCase();
    if (!allowedTypes.includes(fileExt)) {
      return res.status(400).json({
        status: 'error',
        message: 'File type not allowed',
        code: 'INVALID_FILE_TYPE'
      });
    }

    // Save file and update user
    const filePath = `${process.env.USER_AVATAR_UPLOAD_PATH}/${userId}_${Date.now()}.${fileExt}`;

    const updatedUser = await prisma.user.update({
      where: { id: userId },
      data: { avatar: filePath },
      select: { id: true, avatar: true }
    });

    // Audit log
    await prisma.auditLog.create({
      data: {
        userId,
        action: 'AVATAR_UPLOAD',
        resource: 'User',
        resourceId: userId,
        changes: { avatar: filePath },
        ipAddress: req.ip,
        userAgent: req.get('User-Agent'),
      }
    });

    res.json({
      status: 'success',
      data: { user: updatedUser }
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Avatar upload error:', error);
    res.status(500).json({
      status: 'error',
      message: 'Failed to upload avatar',
      code: 'UPLOAD_ERROR'
    });
  }
}
```

## **Shipment Service Implementation Patterns**

### **Core Responsibilities**

- Order and shipment management
- Tracking and status updates
- Courier integration
- Notification handling (SMS/Email)

### **Specific Schema Patterns**

```prisma
// Shipment Service Schema
model Shipment {
  id              String        @id @default(cuid())
  trackingNumber  String        @unique
  referenceNumber String?
  userId          String        // From user service
  clientId        String?       // Multi-tenant support

  // Shipment details
  status          ShipmentStatus @default(CREATED)
  courierPartner  String?
  serviceType     String?
  packageWeight   Float?
  packageValue    Float?
  currency        String        @default("INR")

  // Addresses
  senderAddress   Json          // Address object
  receiverAddress Json          // Address object

  // Tracking
  estimatedDelivery DateTime?
  actualDelivery    DateTime?

  // Metadata
  manifestDate    DateTime?
  paymentMode     PaymentMode   @default(PREPAID)
  createdAt       DateTime      @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime      @updatedAt

  // Relationships
  trackingEvents  TrackingEvent[]
  documents       ShipmentDocument[]
  notifications   Notification[]

  @@map("shipments")
}

model TrackingEvent {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  shipmentId  String
  status      String
  location    String?
  description String?
  timestamp   DateTime @default(now())

  // Relationships
  shipment    Shipment @relation(fields: [shipmentId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@map("tracking_events")
}

enum ShipmentStatus {
  CREATED
  PICKED_UP
  IN_TRANSIT
  OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
  DELIVERED
  RETURNED
  CANCELLED
}

enum PaymentMode {
  PREPAID
  COD
}
```

### **Notification Service Pattern**

```javascript
// services/notificationService.js
class NotificationService {
  static async sendShipmentUpdate(shipmentId, status, userPhone, userEmail) {
    try {
      const shipment = await prisma.shipment.findUnique({
        where: { id: shipmentId },
        select: { trackingNumber: true, referenceNumber: true },
      });

      // SMS notification
      if (userPhone && process.env.SMS_PROVIDER === "msg91") {
        await this.sendSMS(userPhone, {
          trackingNumber: shipment.trackingNumber,
          status: status,
          referenceNumber: shipment.referenceNumber,
        });
      }

      // Email notification
      if (userEmail && process.env.EMAIL_PROVIDER === "sendgrid") {
        await this.sendEmail(userEmail, {
          trackingNumber: shipment.trackingNumber,
          status: status,
          referenceNumber: shipment.referenceNumber,
        });
      }

      // Log notification
      await prisma.notification.create({
        data: {
          shipmentId,
          type: "STATUS_UPDATE",
          channel: "SMS_EMAIL",
